<Legal title="Cookies" updated="2026-10-28">
<p>The site sets no cookies of its own. The only cookies come from Google Analytics.</p>
<p>Visitors from the EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland get these cookies only after clicking "accept". Everywhere else they are set when you arrive, and you can turn them off with "cookie settings" in the footer.</p>

<h2>Google Analytics cookies</h2>
<table class="tbl">
  <thead><tr><th>name</th><th>set by</th><th>purpose</th><th>expires</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>_ga</td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Tells visits apart</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
    <tr><td>_ga_&lt;id&gt;</td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Keeps session state</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Your choice</h2>
<p>Your choice is saved in your browser's local storage, not in a cookie, so the banner doesn't come back on every page. Change it any time with "cookie settings" in the footer. Rejecting deletes the analytics cookies.</p>
<p>Blocking cookies in your browser doesn't break anything on this site.</p>

<h2>Cloudflare</h2>
<p>Cloudflare may set a security cookie (such as <code>__cf_bm</code>) to tell people from bots. It is strictly necessary for security, holds no personal profile, and expires within 30 minutes.</p>

<p>More on data handling: <a href="/privacy">privacy</a>.</p>
</Legal>
